<section class="hero"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Associate</a><span class="sep">›</span><a href="#">Module 8</a><span class="sep">›</span><span>Advanced Patterns</span></div><span class="hero-eyebrow">Module 8 · Lesson 5</span><h1>Advanced Prompt Patterns</h1><p class="hero-sub">Master sophisticated prompt engineering techniques including role-based prompting, multi-turn conversations, retrieval-augmented generation, and self-refinement strategies. Learn how expert practitioners combine multiple techniques to build reliable, scalable LLM applications.</p></section>

<div class="objectives"><h4>Learning Objectives</h4><ul><li>Apply role-based and persona-driven prompting for specialized outputs</li><li>Build multi-turn conversations with context preservation and consistency</li><li>Implement self-refinement and iterative improvement loops</li><li>Combine multiple prompting techniques into sophisticated workflows</li><li>Handle complex reasoning tasks with structured decomposition</li><li>Debug and optimize prompts for production reliability</li></ul></div>

<section class="section" id="role-based"><span class="section-label">Persona &amp; Role</span><h2>Role-Based and Persona-Driven Prompting</h2><p>Assigning personas to the LLM can dramatically improve output quality and consistency. When you tell the model to act as an expert in a specific domain, it activates relevant knowledge patterns and adjusts its communication style appropriately. This is one of the most powerful techniques in prompt engineering.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="im">openai</span> <span class="kw">import</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span>

<span class="va">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span>()

<span class="cm"># Role-based system prompt with detailed expertise definition</span>
<span class="va">system_prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"""You are an expert data scientist with 15 years of experience in machine learning,
statistical modeling, and production systems. You have deep knowledge of:
- Data preprocessing and feature engineering
- Statistical testing and validation
- Production ML deployment and monitoring
- Industry best practices and common pitfalls

When answering questions, provide:
1. Technical explanation with precise terminology
2. Practical code examples when relevant
3. Common mistakes to avoid
4. Real-world context from your experience

Always explain the "why" behind recommendations."""</span>

<span class="va">user_question</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"""How should I approach feature scaling in my preprocessing pipeline?
I have a dataset with features ranging from 0-1, 0-1000, and -100 to 100."""</span>

<span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
    <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
    <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[
        {<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"system"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">system_prompt</span>},
        {<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">user_question</span>}
    ]
)

<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>)</code></pre>

<div class="key-concept"><strong>Key Concept:</strong> The more specific and detailed your role description, the more consistent and expert-like the outputs. Include credentials, experience, and constraints.</div>

<section class="section" id="multi-turn"><span class="section-label">Conversation Management</span><h2>Multi-Turn Conversations and Context</h2><p>Advanced applications require maintaining conversation history and context across multiple exchanges. Learn how to structure multi-turn conversations for coherent, contextual responses while managing token usage efficiently.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="kw">class</span> <span class="fn">ConversationManager</span>:
    <span class="st">"""Manage multi-turn conversations with context and history."""</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">system_prompt</span>, <span class="va">max_history</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">10</span>):
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span>()
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">system_prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">system_prompt</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">messages</span> <span class="op">=</span> []
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">max_history</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">max_history</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">add_context</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">context</span>):
        <span class="st">"""Add contextual information to the system prompt."""</span>
        <span class="va">enhanced_system</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">f"""{self.system_prompt}

CONTEXT:
{context}"""</span>
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">enhanced_system</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">chat</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">user_message</span>, <span class="va">context</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="kw">None</span>):
        <span class="st">"""Send message and get response, maintaining history."""</span>
        <span class="va">system_prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="fn">add_context</span>(<span class="va">context</span>) <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">context</span> <span class="kw">else</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">system_prompt</span>

        <span class="cm"># Add user message to history</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">messages</span>.<span class="fn">append</span>({
            <span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>,
            <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">user_message</span>
        })

        <span class="cm"># Keep only recent messages to manage token usage</span>
        <span class="va">messages_to_send</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">messages</span>[<span class="op">-</span><span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">max_history</span>:]

        <span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
            <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
            <span class="va">system</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">system_prompt</span>,
            <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">messages_to_send</span>
        )

        <span class="va">assistant_message</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">messages</span>.<span class="fn">append</span>({
            <span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"assistant"</span>,
            <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">assistant_message</span>
        })

        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">assistant_message</span>

<span class="cm"># Usage</span>
<span class="va">manager</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">ConversationManager</span>(<span class="st">"You are a Python expert."</span>)
<span class="va">manager</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>(<span class="st">"Explain list comprehensions"</span>)
<span class="va">manager</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>(<span class="st">"How about with nested loops?"</span>)  <span class="cm"># Knows context from previous</span></code></pre>

<section class="section" id="self-refinement"><span class="section-label">Iterative Improvement</span><h2>Self-Refinement and Iterative Improvement</h2><p>Advanced systems ask the LLM to evaluate and improve its own outputs. This technique often produces significantly better results than single-pass generation, especially for complex tasks.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">refine_response</span>(<span class="va">initial_text</span>, <span class="va">criteria</span>, <span class="va">iterations</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">2</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Iteratively refine text based on quality criteria."""</span>
    <span class="va">current_text</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">initial_text</span>

    <span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">i</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="fn">range</span>(<span class="va">iterations</span>):
        <span class="va">evaluation_prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">f"""Evaluate this text against these criteria: {criteria}

Text: {current_text}

Identify specific improvements needed. Then provide an improved version.
Return ONLY the improved text."""</span>

        <span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
            <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
            <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[{<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">evaluation_prompt</span>}],
            <span class="va">temperature</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">0</span>
        )

        <span class="va">current_text</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>

    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">current_text</span>

<span class="cm"># Usage</span>
<span class="va">draft</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">"Machine learning is cool and helps with AI stuff."</span>
<span class="va">refined</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">refine_response</span>(
    <span class="va">draft</span>,
    <span class="st">"clarity, technical accuracy, professional tone"</span>
)</code></pre>

<div class="callout-box tip"><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Self-refinement works best with clear evaluation criteria. The more specific your quality standards, the better the improvements.</div>

<section class="section" id="decomposition"><span class="section-label">Complex Tasks</span><h2>Decomposition and Multi-Step Reasoning</h2><p>Break complex problems into smaller steps. Ask the model to work through each step explicitly, then synthesize results. This approach, called chain-of-thought decomposition, significantly improves accuracy.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">solve_complex_problem</span>(<span class="va">problem</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Solve complex problem by breaking into steps."""</span>

    <span class="cm"># Step 1: Break down the problem</span>
    <span class="va">decompose_prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">f"""Problem: {problem}

Break this into 3-5 concrete, actionable steps. Number them.
Return ONLY the numbered steps."""</span>

    <span class="va">response1</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
        <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
        <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[{<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">decompose_prompt</span>}]
    )
    <span class="va">steps</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">response1</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>

    <span class="cm"># Step 2: Solve each step</span>
    <span class="va">solve_prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">f"""Steps to solve: {steps}

For each step, explain how to accomplish it and any implementation details needed.
Be specific and technical."""</span>

    <span class="va">response2</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
        <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
        <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[{<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">solve_prompt</span>}]
    )
    <span class="va">solutions</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">response2</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>

    <span class="cm"># Step 3: Synthesize final answer</span>
    <span class="va">synthesize_prompt</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="st">f"""Problem: {problem}
Steps and solutions: {solutions}

Provide a comprehensive final answer that synthesizes all steps.
Structure with clear headings and actionable recommendations."""</span>

    <span class="va">response3</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
        <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
        <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[{<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">synthesize_prompt</span>}]
    )

    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">response3</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span></code></pre>

<section class="section" id="expert-workflows"><span class="section-label">Production Workflows</span><h2>Building Expert Workflows with Prompt Chains</h2><p>Combine multiple specialized prompts into a sophisticated workflow where each prompt builds on previous outputs. This is how production LLM systems achieve reliability and quality at scale.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="kw">class</span> <span class="fn">PromptChain</span>:
    <span class="st">"""Chain prompts together for sophisticated multi-step workflows."""</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(<span class="va">self</span>):
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">client</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">OpenAI</span>()
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">results</span> <span class="op">=</span> {}

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">run</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">prompt</span>, <span class="va">name</span>, <span class="va">system</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="kw">None</span>):
        <span class="st">"""Run a prompt step and store result."""</span>
        <span class="va">messages</span> <span class="op">=</span> []
        <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">system</span>:
            <span class="va">messages</span>.<span class="fn">append</span>({<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"system"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">system</span>})
        <span class="va">messages</span>.<span class="fn">append</span>({<span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>, <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">prompt</span>})

        <span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
            <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
            <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">messages</span>
        )

        <span class="va">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">results</span>[<span class="va">name</span>] <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">result</span>
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">result</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">name</span>):
        <span class="st">"""Get a previous result to use in next prompt."""</span>
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">results</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="va">name</span>)

<span class="cm"># Usage: Document summarization with fact extraction</span>
<span class="va">chain</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">PromptChain</span>()

<span class="cm"># Step 1: Summarize document</span>
<span class="va">summary</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">chain</span>.<span class="fn">run</span>(
    <span class="st">f"Summarize in 3-5 sentences: {long_document}"</span>,
    <span class="st">"summary"</span>
)

<span class="cm"># Step 2: Extract facts from summary</span>
<span class="va">facts</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">chain</span>.<span class="fn">run</span>(
    <span class="st">f"""Extract key facts as JSON array from: {chain.get('summary')}
    Format: [{{"fact": "...", "confidence": 0.0-1.0}}]"""</span>,
    <span class="st">"facts"</span>
)

<span class="cm"># Step 3: Generate recommendations based on facts</span>
<span class="va">recommendations</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">chain</span>.<span class="fn">run</span>(
    <span class="st">f"""Based on facts: {chain.get('facts')}
    Provide 3 actionable recommendations."""</span>,
    <span class="st">"recommendations"</span>
)</code></pre>

<div class="callout-box success"><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Store intermediate results and use them to debug. If a later step fails, you can retry with the same earlier output.</div>

<section class="section" id="debugging"><span class="section-label">Optimization &amp; Debugging</span><h2>Prompt Debugging and Optimization</h2><p>Systematically improve prompts by testing different variations and measuring output quality. Build test suites to ensure consistency before deploying to production.</p>

<div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div><pre><code><span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">compare_prompts</span>(<span class="va">prompts</span>, <span class="va">test_cases</span>):
    <span class="st">"""Test multiple prompt variants across test cases."""</span>
    <span class="va">results</span> <span class="op">=</span> {<span class="va">name</span>: [] <span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">name</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">prompts</span>}

    <span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">test_input</span>, <span class="va">expected</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">test_cases</span>:
        <span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">name</span>, <span class="va">prompt_template</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="va">prompts</span>.<span class="fn">items</span>():
            <span class="va">response</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">client</span>.<span class="fn">chat</span>.<span class="fn">completions</span>.<span class="fn">create</span>(
                <span class="va">model</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="st">"gpt-4"</span>,
                <span class="va">messages</span><span class="op">=</span>[{
                    <span class="st">"role"</span>: <span class="st">"user"</span>,
                    <span class="st">"content"</span>: <span class="va">prompt_template</span>.<span class="fn">format</span>(<span class="va">input</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="va">test_input</span>)
                }]
            )

            <span class="va">output</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">response</span>.<span class="fn">choices</span>[<span class="nm">0</span>].<span class="fn">message</span>.<span class="fn">content</span>
            <span class="va">results</span>[<span class="va">name</span>].<span class="fn">append</span>({
                <span class="st">"input"</span>: <span class="va">test_input</span>,
                <span class="st">"output"</span>: <span class="va">output</span>,
                <span class="st">"length"</span>: <span class="fn">len</span>(<span class="va">output</span>)
            })

    <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="va">results</span>

<span class="cm"># Test and compare variants</span>
<span class="va">variants</span> <span class="op">=</span> {
    <span class="st">"basic"</span>: <span class="st">"Explain {input}"</span>,
    <span class="st">"detailed"</span>: <span class="st">"Explain {input} in detail with examples"</span>,
    <span class="st">"expert"</span>: <span class="st">"As a domain expert, explain {input} covering theory, practice, and common pitfalls"</span>
}

<span class="va">test_cases</span> <span class="op">=</span> [
    (<span class="st">"neural networks"</span>, <span class="st">"comprehensive explanation"</span>),
    (<span class="st">"transformers"</span>, <span class="st">"technical depth"</span>)
]

<span class="va">results</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">compare_prompts</span>(<span class="va">variants</span>, <span class="va">test_cases</span>)</code></pre>

<section class="section" id="summary"><span class="section-label">Summary</span><h2>Key Takeaways</h2><ul><li><strong>Role-Based Prompting:</strong> Assigning detailed personas activates specialized knowledge and improves output quality significantly.</li><li><strong>Multi-Turn Conversations:</strong> Maintain message history while managing tokens. Keep recent context but don't overload with old messages.</li><li><strong>Self-Refinement:</strong> Ask models to evaluate and improve their outputs. Multiple iterations typically produce better results than single-pass generation.</li><li><strong>Decomposition:</strong> Break complex problems into explicit steps. Chain-of-thought reasoning improves accuracy and transparency.</li><li><strong>Prompt Chains:</strong> Combine multiple specialized prompts where each builds on previous outputs. Store intermediate results for debugging.</li><li><strong>Testing &amp; Optimization:</strong> Build test suites comparing prompt variants. Systematically improve before production deployment.</li></ul></div>

